/S /H1
/P 96 0 R
/T (Using PC1084 Ginger Root with light-to-medium pressure, layer into the mid-tone transition zones and anywhere aged or oxidized skin is visible. This warm mid-tone suggests natural skin complexity and can be used sparingly around the mouth area, eyes, and ears. Apply short, directional strokes following face contours, blending where appropriate. This step adds richness and depth to mid-tones without darkening them. Layer with transparency rather than heavy coverage. If the face begins to look too warm overall, dial back; if it looks flat and lifeless, add more Ginger Root to the mid-tones.)
/E (Using PC1084 Ginger Root with light-to-medium pressure, layer into the mid-tone transition zones and anywhere aged or oxidized skin is visible. This warm mid-tone suggests natural skin complexity and can be used sparingly around the mouth area, eyes, and ears. Apply short, directional strokes following face contours, blending where appropriate. This step adds richness and depth to mid-tones without darkening them. Layer with transparency rather than heavy coverage. If the face begins to look too warm overall, dial back; if it looks flat and lifeless, add more Ginger Root to the mid-tones.)
