356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 99 0 R
/T (Using PC140 Eggshell with light-to-medium pressure, strengthen highlights on the forehead, outer cheekbone, nose bridge, and any other high-point catch lights. Apply in small, deliberate circular strokes where light hits most directly. Then, using PC938 White with medium-to-heavy pressure, apply specular shine to the very highest points \(cheekbone peak, center of forehead, eye catchlight\). Burnish these areas with firm, circular pressure to create a polished, luminous surface. The goal is to make light areas glow without making them look artificial. Burnishing compresses pigment and creates a glossy, dimensional quality.)
/E (Using PC140 Eggshell with light-to-medium pressure, strengthen highlights on the forehead, outer cheekbone, nose bridge, and any other high-point catch lights. Apply in small, deliberate circular strokes where light hits most directly. Then, using PC938 White with medium-to-heavy pressure, apply specular shine to the very highest points \(cheekbone peak, center of forehead, eye catchlight\). Burnish these areas with firm, circular pressure to create a polished, luminous surface. The goal is to make light areas glow without making them look artificial. Burnishing compresses pigment and creates a glossy, dimensional quality.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
