/Title (Layer PC1023 Cloud Blue into the deepest shadows with very light pressure, focusing on areas where cool ambient light \(from the environment or sky\) would be reflected upward into shadow cavities. This might include the under-cheekbone hollow and under-jaw shadow. Avoid the mouth and nasal areas; focus on sculptural shadow planes. The blue should be barely visible, adding a subtle cool glow without dominating. This creates optical mixing with the underlying warm tones, producing natural shadow color \(green-grey or cool purple-grey\) rather than flat grey. Use tiny circular strokes and allow the underlying layers to show through.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
